{
  "format": "WFScriptPanel",
  "version": 2,
  "description": "Seven-page automated Test Station with project-owned UUT fields, native execution, auto-archived JSON reports and optional manual export.",
  "scriptName": "AutomatedTestStation.js",
  "activePageId": "uut",
  "lifecycle": {
    "initializeEnabled": false,
    "shutdownEnabled": false
  },
  "appearance": {
    "themeMode": "dark",
    "background": "",
    "showDesignGrid": true
  },
  "pages": [
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "name": "00 Test Overview",
      "width": 1320,
      "height": 860,
      "controls": [
        {
          "id": "guideHeading",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "<div align=\"left\" style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;color:#d9e8f4;font-size:12px\"><h2 style=\"color:#7dd3fc\">WFScript | Build and Run Your First Test</h2><p style=\"color:#cbd5e1\">One C++ test definition. One function library. One simple operator Panel.</p></div>",
          "x": 25,
          "y": 18,
          "width": 1264,
          "height": 72,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "textFormat": "Rich Text",
            "wordWrap": true,
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 9
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "guidePurpose",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "<div align=\"left\" style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;color:#d9e8f4;font-size:12px\"><h3 style=\"color:#7dd3fc\">1. Where is the test?</h3><p>The test is a <b>first-class object inside this .wfpanel</b>, not in JavaScript. Open <b>Test Sequence…</b> in the Panel Designer to edit its steps, order, handlers, acceptance limits and total timeout. Save the .wfpanel and reopen it: those exact settings will be loaded.</p></div>",
          "x": 25,
          "y": 105,
          "width": 611,
          "height": 229,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "textFormat": "Rich Text",
            "wordWrap": true,
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 9
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "guideMechanics",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "<div align=\"left\" style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;color:#d9e8f4;font-size:12px\"><h3 style=\"color:#7dd3fc\">2. Who does what?</h3><p><b>Qt/C++:</b> loads and validates the test on Panel startup, schedules steps, checks numeric limits, handles cleanup and records results.<br><b>TestSteps.mjs:</b> each exported function makes one simulated measurement and returns a number.<br><b>OperatorPanel.js:</b> binds Run, Next, Stop and Reset; displays/export reports. <b>No test registration or configuration code.</b></p></div>",
          "x": 656,
          "y": 105,
          "width": 633,
          "height": 229,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "textFormat": "Rich Text",
            "wordWrap": true,
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 9
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "guideSequence",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "<div align=\"left\" style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;color:#d9e8f4;font-size:12px\"><h3 style=\"color:#7dd3fc\">3. Exact sequence</h3><p><b>Setup:</b> 150 ms nonblocking settling.<br><b>Main:</b> V+ 3.301 V (3.25–3.35), V− −3.298 V (−3.35–−3.25), clock 999.8 Hz (990–1010; polled every 10 ms), PWM 50.1% (49–51), finalize.<br><b>Cleanup:</b> restore station. The configured total timeout starts at <b>15,000 ms</b>.</p></div>",
          "x": 25,
          "y": 346,
          "width": 611,
          "height": 338,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "textFormat": "Rich Text",
            "wordWrap": true,
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 9
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "guideOutcomes",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "<div align=\"left\" style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;color:#d9e8f4;font-size:12px\"><h3 style=\"color:#7dd3fc\">4. What to expect</h3><p><b>RUN TEST:</b> all four numeric measurements PASS; final overall state PASSED; Setup/Cleanup actions are DONE.<br><b>STOP (CLEANUP):</b> graceful terminate while a timed step is RUNNING; unfinished Main steps are skipped and Cleanup runs.<br><b>Test a failure:</b> change the PWM value to 47.5 in TestSteps.mjs. The C++ executive compares it with the saved 49–51% range and reports FAIL without changing any Panel code.</p></div>",
          "x": 656,
          "y": 346,
          "width": 633,
          "height": 338,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "textFormat": "Rich Text",
            "wordWrap": true,
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 9
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "guideActions",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "<div align=\"left\" style=\"font-family:Segoe UI;color:#d9e8f4;font-size:12px\"><h3 style=\"color:#7dd3fc\">5. Try editing a test</h3><p>Stop Panel mode → open <b>Test Sequence…</b> → set Total Timeout to 15,000 ms or another value → change the Setup delay or insert a new Main Delay → Save to Panel → save the .wfpanel → start Panel → RUN TEST. The report shows the configured timeout. JSON reports auto-save; open them through Script → Open Test Results Folder. <b>No second configuration exists.</b></p></div>",
          "x": 25,
          "y": 691,
          "width": 1264,
          "height": 153,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "textFormat": "Rich Text",
            "wordWrap": true,
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 9
          }
        }
      ]
    },
